security cameras record the impact  of a sudden explosion in a residential  neighborhood just outside bangkok  the ground shook just like an earthquake  said residents  shattering windows all around the source  a huge chemical factory in somewhat  prakhan on the outskirts of the thai  capital  highly flammable materials used to make  foam packaging  quickly engulfed the complex in flames  that firefighters struggle to contain  we are trying to look for the injured  however the flames are quite high  so it takes quite an effort to look for  people rescuers are also spreading out  because we receive calls  for people who have injuries from  explosions from the extended area  one or two streets away from here there  are reports of falling debris  injuries from debris impacts on faces  and heads  the damage caused by the explosion was  considerable it's estimated the factory  alone has suffered more than 20 million  us dollars worth  70 homes are also seriously affected and  thousands of people have been evacuated  from within a wide radius of the factory  firefighters struggled throughout the  day to bring the blaze under control but  the flammable nature of the chemicals  made it a complicated and dangerous task  at times the flames taking over areas  the firefighters thought they had  under control as the day went on a huge  plume of smoke rose across the area  described by some witnesses as toxic and  visible across bangkok and beyond  when that finally clears there'll be  questions to answer  about the failure to control such  dangerous chemicals  tony chang al jazeera bangkok
 

